WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.594
A living trust is like a container you create

2
00:00:06.594 --> 00:00:10.600
to hold your assets.

3
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.859
You usually wear three hats:

4
00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:16.704
the person who creates it,

5
00:00:16.704 --> 00:00:19.301
the one who manages it,

6
00:00:19.301 --> 00:00:21.444
and, while alive,

7
00:00:21.444 --> 00:00:24.600
the one who benefits.

8
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.718
Then you move assets into it.

9
00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:32.161
This step is called funding,

10
00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:37.100
and it is the part people forget.

11
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.676
If you become unable to manage things,

12
00:00:41.676 --> 00:00:46.270
the successor trustee you chose steps in,

13
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.100
without a court.

14
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.103
When you die,

15
00:00:51.103 --> 00:00:55.689
the trust assets pass to your beneficiaries

16
00:00:55.689 --> 00:00:57.713
as you set out,

17
00:00:57.713 --> 00:01:01.100
often without probate.

18
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.505
Retirement accounts usually stay as they are,

19
00:01:05.505 --> 00:01:08.051
with a beneficiary form.

20
00:01:08.051 --> 00:01:11.045
A trust costs more up front.

21
00:01:11.045 --> 00:01:13.104
And it is revocable,

22
00:01:13.104 --> 00:01:16.100
so you can change it.

23
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:20.388
Wondering if you need one?

24
00:01:20.388 --> 00:01:27.100
Our plan finder is a good place to start.
